{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Darius</b> — Know that this Darius the Mede is not Darius the Persian under whom the House [Temple] was built in the second year of his reign. Now according to the view of the ancients, as I shall explain, Daniel erred in his reckoning. For they said: In the seventh year Esther was taken, and Darius, who was her son, was born in the eighth year of Ahasuerus, and his entire reign was 13 years. Now Jehoahaz reigned 6 years, for in the second year of his reign the House was built. And it is written that Jehoash was seven years old when he reigned, and close to this number was King Josiah. And concerning this Darius it is written that he was 62 years old when he reigned over Chaldea, and it is known that Cyrus captured Babylon, as written in the book of Isaiah. And it is written that Cyrus reigned over Babylon, and after him Ahasuerus reigned, and after Ahasuerus, according to our Sages, Darius the Persian, who was Esther's son, reigned. Therefore, even though it is written 'in the first year of Darius son of Ahasuerus, of the seed of Media,' this is not that Ahasuerus who took Esther, but another. And so was the father of this Darius the Elder, who was the first king of the kings of Media and Persia to reign over the Chaldeans, when Babylon was captured and the kingdom of Chaldea was cut off before the death of Belshazzar. And there is no need to elaborate, for the matter is clear and without doubt, and in the books of the kings of Persia, that this Darius the Elder was the father-in-law of Cyrus, and both of them captured Babylon — for Cyrus was king of Persia and this Darius was king of Media, and it is written: 'Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them.' And Cyrus left his father-in-law over the kingdom of Chaldea, for Cyrus enthroned him, for Cyrus said: 'All the kingdoms of the earth Elohim has given into my hand.' And they reigned at the same time; therefore, when Chaldea fell, Israel went up from Babylon with Zerubbabel, as Cyrus commanded, for he was the great king. Therefore it is written: 'And he and his sons became servants until the reign of the kingdom of Persia.' And the meaning of 'in the first year of Cyrus, when he reigned over Babylon,' is that Israel were there, for he was already king beforehand; therefore Cyrus is called king of Babylon."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's references to biblical kings (Jehoahaz, Jehoash) are left as transmitted; these appear to be midrashic or chronographic traditions and are not smoothed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:12.270558395Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}